# Residual-normalizer analysis for 14.7.67(3–4)

The shared preliminaries construct the literal section kernel D, its residual
D₁ = O²(D ∩ N_G(L)), and the point span E. They establish D ∩ H ≤ T,
C_D(E) ≤ T, and the returning-point residual argument used in the solvable
branch. The proper-overgroup exclusion, D₁/local-Sylow analysis and Thompson
factorization are separate remaining branches; this boundary will assemble
them. No unconditional 14.7.67(3–4) statement is claimed here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript, 1 March 2004, pp.1070–1071.
-/
